From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] installer: seed /etc/locale.conf before package install

The initramfs rpm ships a %transfiletriggerin that runs
"mkinitrd -q /boot/initrd.img-$kver $kver" at the end of the package
transaction performed by _install_packages(). dracut's 20i18n module
checks for $I18N_CONF (/etc/locale.conf) and, when it is missing and
i18n_vars is unset, reports

  dracut[E]: i18n_vars not set!  Please set up i18n_vars in  configuration file.

on the installer console right before the ansible run, and then falls
back to install_all_kbd() - embedding every keymap in the initrd instead
of the target's own.

/etc/locale.conf is only created by m_locale, which runs in the
POST_INSTALL phase, twelve steps after _install_packages(). The file is
therefore guaranteed to be absent while the initrd is generated.

Seed it in _initialize_system(), directly after the filesystem rpm that
provides /etc is installed and before any package transaction can fire
the trigger. m_locale is left untouched: it rewrites the same content
and runs localedef, and it still covers the ostree install path where
_initialize_system() is not called.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
---
 photon_installer/installer.py |  6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/photon_installer/installer.py
+++ b/photon_installer/installer.py
@@ -1304,6 +1304,12 @@
             self.logger.error("Failed to install filesystem rpm")
             self.exit_gracefully()
 
+        # seed /etc/locale.conf for the initrd build; m_locale rewrites it later
+        locale_conf_path = os.path.join(self.photon_root, "etc/locale.conf")
+        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(locale_conf_path), exist_ok=True)
+        with open(locale_conf_path, "w") as locale_conf:
+            locale_conf.write("LANG=en_US.UTF-8\n")
+
     def _mount_special_folders(self):
         for d in ["/proc", "/dev", "/dev/pts", "/sys"]:
             self._mount(d, d, bind=True, create=True)
